{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5fe52zth5rqyq2n5wevhzgkrau5jle3jz7u2fkkh5erezeqotusq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **no divergences found; the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte.**\n\n## Result\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` compiles | ✅ clean, no errors |\n| C `.so` built | ✅ `c_src/build/libdriver.so` |\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: `nm -D` diff | ✅ **empty**; 0 undefined non-libc (`ldd -r` → 0) |\n| Phase B: all 18 `CONFIGS.md` rows | ✅ pass across randomized inputs |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]` (asserted by `cfg_c18_no_binary_target`) |\n| Phase C: all 11 `ERRORS.md` rows | ✅ pass |\n| All feature combos × profiles | ✅ 6/6 configurations, 30/30 tests each |\n\n## What the surface actually is\n\nThe library is one function: `void driver(int)`. It fills `house_t {int floors; int bedrooms; double bathrooms;}` (16 bytes, **no padding**, so `{0}` leaves nothing indeterminate) and hex-dumps its raw bytes via a `static print_hex`. So:\n\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — mechanical grep found **zero** `return`/`assert`/`NULL`/`errno`/`#if`. There is no error channel at all; all 2^32 `int` values are valid. The 11 rows instead pin what the C *does* with each boundary (INT_MIN/MAX, `-1`, unsigned `0x80000000` wraparound through the FFI slot, out-of-range enum-like ints, embedded NUL bytes) and record that NULL-pointer/bad-length rows are structurally unreachable — no pointers in the public API, and `print_hex`'s `len` is hardcoded `sizeof(house_t)`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — no options/flags/`#ifdef`s/globals exist, and `driver` *is* the lowest-level export (`print_hex` is file-local, absent from `nm -D`). Rows therefore enumerate input *shapes*: every single-bit position, bit-run boundaries, endianness probes, all 256 one-byte values, 6k+ seeded-random values, plus statelessness and bulk-stream equivalence.\n\n## Test design notes\n\n`driver` returns `void`, so its only observable behavior is stdout. `tests/common/mod.rs` `dup2`s fd 1 to a temp file around each call and `fflush(NULL)`s — both `.so`s share the process's libc `stdout`, and the Rust lib deliberately imports the same `printf`. Both libraries are loaded with `libloading` under `RTLD_LOCAL`, so the colliding `driver` symbol resolves per-handle; the Rust side is **only** ever reached through `dlsym`, exercising the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper.\n\n`tests/differential.rs` also verifies parity in the other direction: `print_hex`/`house_t` must stay *un*exported in Rust, matching C's `static` linkage.\n\n## Files added\n\n```\ntranslation/SYMBOLS.md  ERRORS.md  CONFIGS.md\ntranslation/tests/differential.rs   (30 tests)\ntranslation/tests/common/mod.rs     (harness + seeded xorshift64* PRNG)\ntranslation/run_all_features.sh     (C build + symbol diff + tests × all combos × release/debug)\ntranslation/.cargo/config.toml      (RUST_TEST_THREADS=1)\ntranslation/Cargo.toml              (+ libloading dev-dep)\n```\n\nTwo things to flag:\n- **`.cargo/config.toml` pins `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`.** fd 1 is process-global, so parallel tests let libtest's own progress lines land *inside* a capture window — that caused a spurious failure on the first run. Single-threading is a correctness requirement of this harness, not a preference.\n- **`--offline` is required here.** The sandbox has no crates.io egress; `libloading 0.8.9` resolved from the local `~/.cargo` cache, and `run_all_features.sh` hardcodes `--offline` for that reason.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified — only a `build/` directory was created in it, as the task's build instructions require."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1274,"cache_read_input_tokens":59482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1274,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"pare